<title>USA: AirWays unit March load factor decreases.</title>
<headline>AirWays unit March load factor decreases.</headline>
<dateline>ORLANDO, Fla. 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>AirWays Corp Monday said the March 1997 load factor for its jet subsidiary, AirTran Airways, decreased 3.4 percent to 73.1 percent from 76.7 percent in March 1996.</p>
<p>			    Mar '97	   Mar '96	  % Change</p>
<p> Passengers Carried:  119,963	   115,609	  +3.78%</p>
<p>Available seat miles (000):</p>
<p>			    138,015	   134,029	  +2.97%</p>
<p>Revenue passenger miles (000):</p>
<p>			    100,945	   102,683	  -1.69%</p>
<p>Load Factor:		73.1%	     76.7%     -3.4 pts.</p>
<p>					   Year-to-Date</p>
<p>				    3 months ended Mar 31, 1997</p>
<p>			     YTD97		YTD96	  % Change</p>
<p> Passengers Carried: 280,022	   264,383	  +5.92%</p>
<p> ASMs (000):	   349,970	   355,955	  -1.68%</p>
<p> RPMs (000):	   234,500	   234,476	   +.01%</p>
<p> Load Factor:	    67.0%	     65.9%     +1.1 pts.</p>
</text>
